{"content":"q28.\n\n**Runners the server actually starts** — all wiring lives in `Server.startBackgroundRunners` (`server/server.go:153-174`), called from `Server.Start` (`server/server.go:129`):\n\n- **s3presign runner (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`)** — started twice-over: one synchronous `RunOnce(ctx)` at boot (`server/server.go:163`), then a long-lived goroutine on `Run(s3Context)` driven by a `time.NewTicker` of `runnerInterval = 12h` (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27,30`). Each tick re-presigns S3 attachment URLs whose `LastPresignedTime` is older than 4 days (`runner.go:85-91`). Cancelled via its own `context.CancelFunc` registered in `backgroundRunnerCancels` and awaited through `backgroundRunnerWG` on shutdown (`server/server.go:156-171`, `176-201`).\n\nThat is the **only** entry in `startBackgroundRunners` — no other runner is launched there.\n\nAdjacent periodic goroutines that exist but are not \"runners\" started by `startBackgroundRunners`:\n\n- **store cache cleanup loops** — three of them, spawned implicitly by `cache.New` (`store/cache/cache.go:83`) when the store is constructed (`store/store.go:51-53`); driven by a ticker on `CleanupInterval = 5m` (`store/cache/cache.go:201`, `store/store.go:42`). Request-path infrastructure, not scheduled work.\n- **SSE heartbeat ticker** — per-connection, 30s (`server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:17,64`). Driven by an inbound client connection, not by the scheduler.\n- **fire-and-forget goroutines** for webhook dispatch (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:44`), email send (`internal/email/email.go:18`), and PAT last-used recording (`server/auth/authenticator.go:180`) — event-triggered, no schedule.\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:** `internal/scheduler` — a full cron implementation (expression parser `internal/scheduler/parser.go`, job registry `internal/scheduler/job.go`, scheduler loop with timezone support and middleware `internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `internal/scheduler/middleware.go`) — is **not used by the server at all**. Its only importers in the repo are its own tests: `internal/scheduler/example_test.go:10` and `internal/scheduler/integration_test.go:13`. The code graph returns a certified zero for callers of `scheduler.New` and `Scheduler.Start` outside the package. Note also that `server/runner/memopayload` has a `Runner`/`RunOnce` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:19,27`) with **no caller anywhere** (certified zero) — only its exported helper `RebuildMemoPayload` is used, inline in the memo service (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447`). So the payload-rebuild runner is dormant scaffolding too.","iteration":14,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
